{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Would that we had died.</b> That we would die; and it is not a noun like מִיתָתֵנוּ, but rather like עֲשׂוֹתֵנוּ, חֲנוֹתֵנוּ, שׁוּבֵנוּ — to do, us; to camp, us; to return, us; to die, us. Its Targum is לְוַי דְּמִיתְנָא — ״לוּ מַתְנוּ״ (Numbers 14:2): would that we had been dead."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:36.989676512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}